# Isaac Robot - Articulated Cameras with UDM Worldgraph

## System Design

**Articulated cameras** (pan-tilt servos) → **UDM worldgraph** (digital twin) → **Virtual sensors** (any config)

### Key Concepts
- Real sensors (moving) project INTO worldgraph
- Worldgraph is canonical representation (ground truth)
- Virtual sensors render FROM worldgraph (simulation, planning, models)
- Enables pre-trained models, offline RL, sensor-independent planning

### Components
- **robot-control** (one container): Chassis, cameras, servos, kinematics, SLAM, worldgraph
- Future: VLA inference, high-level planner (operate on worldgraph, not raw sensors)

## Calibration

### Fixture-Based (One-Time)
- Camera intrinsics (per camera, checkerboard)
- Kinematic chain (base → pan → tilt → camera, marker-based)
- Servo zero positions (homing routine)

### Auto-Calibration (Runtime)
- Odometry (SLAM ground truth)
- IMU biases (zero-velocity updates)
- Worldgraph consistency (multi-view fusion)

Tool: `./calibrate.sh [command]`

## Architecture

```
Cameras (pan-tilt) → Forward Kinematics → World Pose
                           ↓
                  Depth + RGB + Pose
                           ↓
                   UDM Worldgraph (TSDF)
                           ↓
                  Inverse Rendering
                           ↓
              Virtual Sensors (any config)
                           ↓
                  Models/Planning/Training
```

## Files

```
/
├── setup-host.sh              # Minimal host (drivers, Docker, GPU, PTP)
├── deploy.sh                  # Container management
├── calibrate.sh               # Calibration tool
├── docker-compose.yml         # Service definition
├── docker/
│   ├── Dockerfile.robot-control
│   └── entrypoint.sh
├── README.md                  # This design
├── SETUP.md                   # Setup guide
└── docs/
    ├── ARCHITECTURE.md        # Complete architecture
    ├── CALIBRATION.md         # Calibration guide
    ├── SSD_MIGRATION.md       # NVMe setup
    └── RECOVERY.md            # Recovery
```

## Rules

- Container-first: All robot code in containers
- Worldgraph-centric: Canonical representation, not raw sensors
- Autonomous services: Each container independent
- Minimal documentation: README, SETUP, ARCHITECTURE, CALIBRATION only

## Development

```bash
docker compose build
docker compose restart
docker compose logs -f
docker exec -it isaac-robot-control bash
```

## Storage

- `/data/config/` - Calibration files (synced)
- `/data/worldgraph/` - TSDF maps
- `/data/logs/` - Runtime logs (synced)
- `/data/sessions/` - Calibration sessions
